    "factsheet": [
        {
            "heading": "About the house",
            "paragraphs": [
                "This family home has evolved gradually over many years through experimentation with reclaimed materials, handmade ceramics and creative reuse. Rather than undertaking a single large renovation, each room has been thoughtfully transformed using salvaged furniture, reclaimed cupboards and broken tiles, creating bespoke kitchens, bathrooms and mosaic details.\nThe ceramic elements throughout the house, including sinks, lamps, tiles, planters and decorative objects, were designed and made by the owner, demonstrating how handmade pieces can become part of everyday architecture and interiors.\nVisitors will discover a home where sustainability, craftsmanship and creativity come together, and will have the opportunity to learn about the renovation process, ceramic making and the design decisions behind the project."
            ]
        }
    ],
